+# Tasks
+
+## 1. Persistence layer
+
+- [x] 1.1 Add `OrderRepository.applyCoupon(orderId, couponCode, discountCents, finalAmountCents, createdAt)` that runs, inside `BEGIN`/`COMMIT` with `ROLLBACK` on error, the order update, the `coupon_redemptions` insert, and the `coupons.used_count` increment; verify with a focused test that a successful call updates all three records and that a forced failure leaves none changed
+- [x] 1.2 Add any read helpers the service needs (e.g. redemption count by code) to `repositories/`, keeping all SQL in the repository layer; verify by asserting the helper reflects rows inserted by 1.1
+
+## 2. Business rules
+
+- [x] 2.1 Implement `computeDiscount(order, coupon)` in `OrderService` (FIXED value, PERCENT floored, `maxDiscountCents` cap, cap at order amount); verify unit tests cover AC-02, AC-03, AC-04, AC-05
+- [x] 2.2 Implement `OrderService.applyCoupon(id, body)` with request validation, code normalization, and the ten-condition error precedence using the injected `Clock`; verify tests cover each error code and the precedence cases (`ORDER_NOT_FOUND` before `COUPON_NOT_FOUND`, `COUPON_ALREADY_APPLIED` before `COUPON_NOT_FOUND`)
+
+## 3. HTTP layer
+
+- [x] 3.1 Register `POST /orders/:id/apply-coupon` in `routes/orders.ts`, parsing the id and passing the body through; verify `app.request("POST", "/orders/1/apply-coupon", { couponCode })` reaches the service and returns 200 with the updated order
+
+## 4. Acceptance tests
+
+- [x] 4.1 Add tests to `tests/` covering AC-01 through AC-10, including normalization (`" save20 "`), `now == validFrom` success, `now == validUntil` expiry, and amount equality at the minimum; verify `npm test` passes
+- [x] 4.2 Add tests asserting rejections leave the order, `used_count`, and `coupon_redemptions` unchanged; verify the assertions pass against the real `Db`
+
+## 5. Verification
+
+- [x] 5.1 Run `npm run build` and confirm the type check passes with no errors
+- [x] 5.2 Run `npm test` and confirm all existing and new tests pass
+- [x] 5.3 Confirm no existing test files, no schema in `db.ts`, and no dependencies were modified
+
+## Workflow follow-up
+
+- Archive the change after the project's review requirements are satisfied.
+- Verify the archived result under `openspec/changes/archive/`.
